<!-- Further Content Section -->
<div class="container" style="margin-top: 3rem; margin-bottom: 3rem; padding-bottom: 40px;">
  <h2>More About Classic Car Auctions in the UK</h2>
  <p>
    Classic car auctions offer enthusiasts and collectors the chance to discover rare vehicles and unique finds. Whether you're a first-time bidder or a seasoned expert, attending UK classic car auctions is an exciting way to experience the automotive world. Get tips on auction registration, bidding strategies, and what to expect at your next classic car auction.
  </p>

  <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-size: 1.8rem; font-weight: 600;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <p style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; font-size: 1.1rem; color: #555;">Find answers to common questions about classic car auctions in the UK.</p>

    <div class="faq-accordion">
      <!-- FAQ Item 1 -->
      <div class="faq-item" x-data="{ open: false }">
        <button @click="open = !open" class="faq-question">
          <span>How do I find upcoming classic car auctions in the UK?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" :class="{ 'rotated': open }" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
        </button>
        <div x-show="open" x-transition class="faq-answer">
          <p>Use our <a href="https://classiccarclubs.uk/auctions/">classic car auctions</a> calendar to see all scheduled events and locations across the country. Our regularly updated calendar includes auction dates, viewing times, and direct links to auction houses throughout the United Kingdom.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ Item 2 -->
      <div class="faq-item" x-data="{ open: false }">
        <button @click="open = !open" class="faq-question">
          <span>What is the typical buyer's premium at UK classic car auctions?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" :class="{ 'rotated': open }" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
        </button>
        <div x-show="open" x-transition class="faq-answer">
          <p>Most UK auction houses charge a buyer's premium between 5-15% of the hammer price, plus VAT. This fee varies between auction houses, with some online auctions charging as little as 5% and traditional in-person auctions typically charging 10-15% plus VAT.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ Item 3 -->
      <div class="faq-item" x-data="{ open: false }">
        <button @click="open = !open" class="faq-question">
          <span>Can I inspect a classic car before bidding at an auction?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" :class="{ 'rotated': open }" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
        </button>
        <div x-show="open" x-transition class="faq-answer">
          <p>Yes, most UK auction houses offer dedicated viewing days prior to the auction where you can thoroughly inspect vehicles and review their documentation. These preview days are essential for assessing condition and verifying the vehicle's history before placing a bid.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ Item 4 -->
      <div class="faq-item" x-data="{ open: false }">
        <button @click="open = !open" class="faq-question">
          <span>What documents should I check when viewing a classic car at auction?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" :class="{ 'rotated': open }" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
        </button>
        <div x-show="open" x-transition class="faq-answer">
          <p>Always examine the vehicle's V5C registration document, MOT history, service records, and any restoration documentation. Additionally, look for original handbooks, previous owner correspondence, and heritage certificates that confirm the car's provenance and authenticity.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ Item 5 -->
      <div class="faq-item" x-data="{ open: false }">
        <button @click="open = !open" class="faq-question">
          <span>What bidding options are available at classic car auctions in the UK?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" :class="{ 'rotated': open }" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
        </button>
        <div x-show="open" x-transition class="faq-answer">
          <p>Most auction houses offer multiple bidding methods including in-person attendance, telephone bidding, online live bidding, and commission (absentee) bidding where the auction house places bids on your behalf up to your specified maximum.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ Item 6 -->
      <div class="faq-item" x-data="{ open: false }">
        <button @click="open = !open" class="faq-question">
          <span>How do I register to bid at a classic car auction?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" :class="{ 'rotated': open }" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
        </button>
        <div x-show="open" x-transition class="faq-answer">
          <p>Registration typically requires proof of identity (passport or driving license), proof of address (utility bill), and in some cases, a deposit or bank details. Many auction houses require registration at least 24-48 hours before the event, particularly for remote bidding.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ Item 7 -->
      <div class="faq-item" x-data="{ open: false }">
        <button @click="open = !open" class="faq-question">
          <span>What happens after I win a bid at a classic car auction?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" :class="{ 'rotated': open }" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
        </button>
        <div x-show="open" x-transition class="faq-answer">
          <p>After winning, you'll typically need to pay a deposit immediately (often by card) and settle the full balance within 24-48 hours. You'll receive an invoice detailing the hammer price, buyer's premium, and any applicable VAT. Most auction houses will retain the V5C and process the ownership transfer on your behalf.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ Item 8 -->
      <div class="faq-item" x-data="{ open: false }">
        <button @click="open = !open" class="faq-question">
          <span>How do I transport my classic car after an auction?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" :class="{ 'rotated': open }" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
        </button>
        <div x-show="open" x-transition class="faq-answer">
          <p>Most auction houses can arrange transportation through partner companies, though this comes at an additional cost. Alternatively, you can arrange your own transport or drive the vehicle away yourself once payment has been cleared and insurance is in place.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ Item 9 -->
      <div class="faq-item" x-data="{ open: false }">
        <button @click="open = !open" class="faq-question">
          <span>Are there specialists who can inspect a classic car before I bid?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" :class="{ 'rotated': open }" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
        </button>
        <div x-show="open" x-transition class="faq-answer">
          <p>Yes, there are professional classic car inspection services throughout the UK who can attend auction viewing days on your behalf. These experts provide detailed condition reports and can advise on potential issues, helping you make an informed bidding decision if you cannot attend in person.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ Item 10 -->
      <div class="faq-item" x-data="{ open: false }">
        <button @click="open = !open" class="faq-question">
          <span>What should I know about VAT when buying a classic car at auction?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" :class="{ 'rotated': open }" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
        </button>
        <div x-show="open" x-transition class="faq-answer">
          <p>Most classic cars sold at auction are subject to the Auctioneer's Margin Scheme, meaning VAT cannot be reclaimed even by VAT-registered businesses. Additionally, VAT is always charged on the buyer's premium. Some vehicles may also have VAT on the hammer price, particularly if imported from outside the UK, so check the auction catalog carefully for VAT status.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div> <!-- .faq-accordion -->
  </div> <!-- .faq-section -->
</div>

